    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DzC1zdwykGbjEqSNPXeWXk)_\n\n## Merge order\n- Independent; touches only the `fish` package, `.gitignore` and `README.org`.\n- Branch is `481-fisher-setup`, number-prefixed as the PR number was known in advance.\n\n## Changes\n- `fish/.config/fish/fish_plugins`: lists only `jorgebucaran/fisher`.\n- `fish/.config/fish/functions/fisher-bootstrap.fish`: run by hand, never at startup.\n  - If fisher is missing, downloads `fisher.fish` with `curl -fsSL` to a temp file, sources it.\n  - Then `fisher update` (installs all of `fish_plugins`), or `fisher install jorgebucaran/fisher` if there is no list.\n  - If fisher exists already, it only runs `fisher update`.\n  - Optional argument: a tag or branch of fisher instead of `main`.\n- `.gitignore`: ignores `completions/` and `functions/fisher.fish` of the fish package.\n- `README.org`, section \"Fish plugins with fisher\": new machine, add, update, remove, restore, and how it fits with Stow.\n- No CHANGELOG edit (the nightly tidy writes it); no conflict with `config.fish`, `conf.d/` or `functions/` files already in the package.\n\n## Stow notes\n- `.stowrc` has `--no-folding`, so plugin files land in `~/.config/fish/{functions,conf.d,completions}` as real files, not in `~/dotfiles`.\n- `fish_variables` is tracked and will hold fisher's `_fisher_*` universal variables; docs say not to commit those lines. Untracking `fish_variables` would be a separate change.\n\n## Not tested\n- No `fish` or fisher in the container: the function was only read, not run or syntax-checked.\n- Network download of fisher not tried.\n- Fisher writing to `fish_plugins` through the Stow symlink not tried.\n\n## Manual testing\n- [ ] `cd ~/dotfiles && git fetch origin 481-fisher-setup && git checkout 481-fisher-setup`, then `stow fish` (links `fish_plugins` and `fisher-bootstrap.fish`) (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Open a new fish: no download, no new output at startup\n- [ ] `fisher-bootstrap`: downloads fisher, then `fisher list` shows `jorgebucaran/fisher` (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `git -C ~/dotfiles status`: clean except for your own changes (no plugin files in the repo)\n- [ ] Run `fisher-bootstrap` again: says fisher is installed and runs `fisher update`\n- [ ] `fisher install jorgebucaran/nvm.fish`: appended to `~/dotfiles/fish/.config/fish/fish_plugins` (the symlink was kept); `fisher remove` removes it again\n- [ ] Edge case: `fisher-bootstrap` with no network: prints `could not download`, fish still usable\n- [ ] Regression: prompt, `emacs-pr --help`, `zoxide` and the greeting work as before\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main` and `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 481-fisher-setup`.\n- Optionally `fisher remove jorgebucaran/fisher` and delete `~/.config/fish/functions/fisher.fish`, `_fisher_*` lines in `fish_variables`.\n- Restart fish.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBSvN6Sz9QDy9WaQCS)_",
